{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/788430-potential-saga-design-sekhem-modification-question","id":788430,"title":"Potential Saga Design & Sekhem Modification Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-17T18:03:49-08:00","id":788430,"title":"Potential Saga Design & Sekhem Modification Question","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> So I have this really nifty idea to run a saga in which the players time jump through the life span of the Arisen. This isn't time magic, the actual characters go through life from past to present one moment and step at a time. Rather its adventure jumps, leading to missions and projects and stuff being roleplayed from different time periods in a haphazard and random order. So the first session might be in the modern day with 100+ experience characters and then the second session (or upon the completion of the mission) might be say the same set of characters but in Roman times, with only 50 exp (or something). As I said, its the same characters, they are not time jumping, rather the players are playing their character's adventurers in the wrong order. The really cool thing is that random one liners or one-off mentions could actually become plot hooks for an entire period adventure to take place (the two Arisen talking to each other about the time in China where they did that thing with the spoon, you know what never mind we promised never to talk about it) could transform into an adventure in China at some period moment where events unfold to showcase that spoon.<br /> <br /> To do this really nifty (though complex, I know) idea I would need to keep the Arisen characters awake throughout time rather than having them go to sleep and then wake up and stuff. I know that this sort of idea might change some of the themes and stuff of the game, which in all truth I am fine with. I have no issue with adding elements from say the Purified from Immortals to make the template more to my liking, but the biggest hurdle I have is the whole Sekhem nature since as an element it is connected with the Pillars, Affinities, and Utterances. So I was wondering if anybody had any ideas or means or written up methods of changing the way Sekhem, the Descent, and the Sothis Cycle works. I would rather have the power trait be somewhat similar to others (go from 1 to 10 rather than the opposite) and I want the Arisen to be permanently awake rather than just appear during certain times.<br /> <br /> My second general question is that I don't really like the fact that the Arisen cannot create magically powered items, relics and stuff. So I was wondering if anybody had any ideas on what I would need to add or change or effect to provide me with a set of tools that could allow the Arisen themselves in-character to build the various relic categories that are described in the text.<br /> <br /> Thank you for any constructive commentary, thoughts or help. I appreciate the assistance.<br /> <br /> (I will note the things I am interested in changing are things that I have been interested in changing since the very first moment I read the book when it was released. I find a lot of things in this new Mummy to be pretty good and interesting, but the nature of the Descent and the Sothis Cycle and the chains that bind the Arisen are not among them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T18:29:47-08:00","id":788442,"title":"","content":"You'll want to read Sothis Ascends; it offers advice on a chronicle that jumps throughout time. One thing it suggests is keeping experience progression linear (so if you do a scene in the present and then a scene in the 1500s, the characters are just as advanced) in order to save yourself book-keeping and to leave the Arisens curious about the flow of time.<br /> <br /> As for not being able to create new Relics... that's a pretty significant element of the setting. In life, the Guild members who were to become Arisen crafted magical works of art; losing that gift is one of the great tragedies of Arisen existence. I'd urge you to reconsider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T18:53:35-08:00","id":788454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/788430-potential-saga-design-sekhem-modification-question?p=788442#post788442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll want to read Sothis Ascends; it offers advice on a chronicle that jumps throughout time. One thing it suggests is keeping experience progression linear (so if you do a scene in the present and then a scene in the 1500s, the characters are just as advanced) in order to save yourself book-keeping and to leave the Arisens curious about the flow of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its funny while I glanced through that section in Sothis Ascends I didn't give it the attention it deserves. So upon reading it over and stuff your right its pretty cool and a nice set of advise on how to go about such a thing and stuff.<br /> <br /> Its kind of Doctor Who with the Arisen. In that though the character's life is in a straight line the history of the world perceives it out of order (so characters might find talk of the battle that was fought in the past but that they hadn't fought yet).<br /> <br /> Its a very interesting way to go about it and one that I have to think about.<br /> <br /> Because really it begs the question what or who is allowing this set of Arisen to do this transcendent adventure thing, and what does it mean and what it is for, and who is the mystery behind it. And what is that seen at the corner of the eye upon moving between points. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for not being able to create new Relics... that's a pretty significant element of the setting. In life, the Guild members who were to become Arisen crafted magical works of art; losing that gift is one of the great tragedies of Arisen existence. I'd urge you to reconsider. </div> </div> </div>Its not one of the things I like honestly. I really think the loss of their ability to craft ruins things rather than enhances things. Especially coming from previous Mummy like I did where relic creation was a core element and one of the features I really liked. So the ability to craft would be something that I would want to bring back. Its the same with the whole removal of Descent, I dislike that change.<br /> <br /> Its like the whole mummy being dead dead (like vampires), I prefer them being dead when dead and alive when alive as part of the supernatural nature of their existence. But that is a quick thing to change and modify, just by adding some elements of the Purified template.<br /> <br /> ...Though I could totally see Descent representing the energy gathered to move through time and space and thus is not entirely under their control. It changes what it is, and removes the Sothic Turn, but it keeps the mechanics. hmmm<br /> <br /> I really do appreciate the thoughts it actually helps to motivate me to think about this further. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}